  "challenge": "The reject overweights FR-003 and treats an unknown vendor as fabricated, but the catalog evidence cuts the other way: WidgetA/GadgetX/WidgetB unit prices match get_item_reference exactly ($250/$750/$500), which is the opposite of typical fraud inflation. PO-001 is explicitly a manager-approval threshold, not a pay bar, and IN-003 is the same stock-planning flag as corpus INV-1013\u2014operational, not proof of a fake invoice. VN-001 policy frames unknown vendors as an onboarding/fraud-entry risk to investigate, and zero history is exactly what a first-time payee looks like; FR-003 is only MEDIUM. Nothing in the packet closes off a legitimate new-vendor read, so the right disposition is ESCALATE for vendor verification and approval, not hard REJECT.",
  "proposed_outcome": "ESCALATE",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["VN-001", "FR-003", "PO-001", "IN-003"]
}
